'' A PAREN-LESS CALL AS THE BASE OF A MEMBER ACCESS IS A CALL. Measured: fbc emits
'' 'vr = MK( ); TMP = vr;' for 'mk.ticks' -- exactly the code it emits for
'' 'mk( ).ticks', which is the whole difference between the two spellings.
''
'' LowerAddr was asked for the address of a PROCEDURE and gave its CODE address, and
'' the field offset was applied to that: 'mk.ticks' read the function's own bytes as
'' a struct. It lowered, it verified, and nothing declined.
''
'' The QUALIFIED spelling 'T.StaticFn' is the same rule and was not read at all --
'' chrono/core.bas writes 'DateTime.MaxValue.Day' eleven times and lost 31 statements
'' to it. A PROPERTY is handled before this, so the only member form that arrives is
'' a real procedure.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/parenless-call-base.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0 statements not lowered
'' EXPECT-NOT: func.addr
'' GOLDEN: expected/parenless-call-base.out
